The names and calls WLED 16.0.1 uses that Arduino-ESP32 3 and ESP-IDF 5.5 changed, for the
trial build on the newer USB software, whose USB host knows hubs.

Every change is held by ESP_IDF_VERSION_MAJOR >= 5, so the build known good, on ESP-IDF 4.4,
compiles the same code as before, only some of it on other lines:

- wled00/src/dependencies/network/Network.h: WLED's global Network takes the name
  WLEDNetwork, as Arduino-ESP32 3 has a global Network of its own.
- wled00/bus_manager.cpp: the PWM outputs use ledcAttachChannel and ledcDetach, which take
  the place of ledcSetup, ledcAttachPin and ledcDetachPin.
- wled00/util.cpp: SHA-1 by the calls without _ret of the newer mbedTLS; esp_chip_info.h
  and esp_mac.h included; the chip's revision as `revision`; the device's fingerprint
  without the legacy ADC driver's calibration, as ESP-IDF 5 stops a firmware at its start
  that holds the legacy ADC driver beside the new one Arduino-ESP32 3 uses.

- wled00/wled.cpp: the static address is compared as a number, as Arduino-ESP32 3 takes
  the literal 0U for a null byte pointer and reads through it.
- wled00/network.cpp and wled00/src/dependencies/e131/ESPAsyncE131.cpp: lwIP's core is
  locked around its raw API and igmp_joingroup, which ESP-IDF 5 asserts at the first call.

The usermod cannot do this from outside: these are WLED's own sources, which must compile
before any usermod runs.

diff --git a/wled00/bus_manager.cpp b/wled00/bus_manager.cpp
index 1ba808d..6123608 100644
--- a/wled00/bus_manager.cpp
+++ b/wled00/bus_manager.cpp
@@ -452,8 +452,12 @@ BusPwm::BusPwm(const BusConfig &bc)
       pinMode(_pins[i], OUTPUT);
       #else
       unsigned channel = _ledcStart + i;
+      #if defined(ESP_IDF_VERSION_MAJOR) && ESP_IDF_VERSION_MAJOR >= 5
+      ledcAttachChannel(_pins[i], _frequency, _depth - (dithering*4), channel);
+      #else
       ledcSetup(channel, _frequency, _depth - (dithering*4)); // with dithering _frequency doesn't really matter as resolution is 8 bit
       ledcAttachPin(_pins[i], channel);
+      #endif
       // LEDC timer reset credit @dedehai
       uint8_t group = (channel / 8), timer = ((channel / 2) % 4); // same fromula as in ledcSetup()
       ledc_timer_rst((ledc_mode_t)group, (ledc_timer_t)timer); // reset timer so all timers are almost in sync (for phase shift)
@@ -623,8 +627,12 @@ void BusPwm::deallocatePins() {
     #ifdef ESP8266
     digitalWrite(_pins[i], LOW); //turn off PWM interrupt
     #else
+    #if defined(ESP_IDF_VERSION_MAJOR) && ESP_IDF_VERSION_MAJOR >= 5
+    if (_ledcStart < WLED_MAX_ANALOG_CHANNELS) ledcDetach(_pins[i]);
+    #else
     if (_ledcStart < WLED_MAX_ANALOG_CHANNELS) ledcDetachPin(_pins[i]);
     #endif
+    #endif
   }
   #ifdef ARDUINO_ARCH_ESP32
   PinManager::deallocateLedc(_ledcStart, numPins);
